+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="early">
+    <h2>Apply before you defend</h2>
+    <p class="lede">These are postdoctoral fellowships, which is why they are usually filed under
+      "not yet". But the application happens while you are still a student, and the deadlines sit twelve
+      to eighteen months before the money starts. Treating them as postdoc business is the most common
+      way a senior student loses a year of independent salary support.</p>
+    <div class="tablewrap">
+      <table class="plain">
+        <thead><tr><th>Award</th><th>What it requires of a student</th><th class="nw">Deadline</th></tr></thead>
+        <tbody>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>Life Sciences Research Foundation</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">Open-field, three years of postdoctoral support. Non-US citizens must
+              work in a US laboratory.</span></td>
+            <td>You may apply <strong>before defending</strong>, provided the degree is in hand by the award's
+              August activation, and within five years of the degree. Applicants in HHMI Investigator
+              labs are ineligible for the current cycle.</td>
+            <td class="nw">1 October<br /><span class="sub">references 1 November</span></td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>Jane Coffin Childs Memorial Fund</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">Any citizenship; non-US citizens must be hosted at a US institution.</span></td>
+            <td>PhD candidates are eligible so long as the degree <strong>confers before the fellowship
+              starts</strong>. No more than twelve months of postdoctoral experience.</td>
+            <td class="nw">1 February</td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>Schmidt Science Fellows</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">Requires a deliberate pivot into a new discipline; placement anywhere in
+              the world.</span></td>
+            <td>The defence must fall inside a stated window roughly a year wide, and <strong>your
+              PhD-awarding institution must nominate you</strong> and must itself be a nominating partner.
+              Internal competitions run about a year before the defence.</td>
+            <td class="nw">Nominations in spring<br /><span class="sub">institution-internal first</span></td>
+          </tr>
+        </tbody>
+      </table>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="dept">
+    <h2>Prizes, and the awards someone else has to submit</h2>
+    <p class="lede">These cannot be applied to directly, or cannot be applied to alone. The nomination
+      calendar runs months ahead of the sponsor's deadline, which is how departments quietly forfeit
+      slots they are entitled to. One internal call issued in early September covers the autumn cluster;
+      anything later misses the first of them.</p>
+    <div class="tablewrap">
+      <table class="plain">
+        <thead><tr><th>Award</th><th>Route</th><th>Internal call</th><th class="nw">Sponsor cycle</th></tr></thead>
+        <tbody>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>Harold M. Weintraub Graduate Student Award</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">Fred Hutch. Up to twelve awardees present their thesis work at a
+              symposium; expenses are covered by the Weintraub&ndash;Groudine Fellowship. No cash prize is
+              published. For students at or near the end of the thesis.</span></td>
+            <td>Department chair or designee &mdash; <strong>one nomination per department or programme</strong></td>
+            <td>Early-to-mid September, so a committee can pick the single nominee</td>
+            <td class="nw">Opens 1 October<br />closes early December</td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>Regeneron Prize for Creative Innovation</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">$25,000 to each graduate winner, $5,000 to each finalist, $5,000 to the
+              winner's institution for a seminar. Judged on a forward-looking "dream project" proposal
+              rather than on completed work.</span></td>
+            <td>The institution &mdash; <strong>up to two graduate nominees</strong>, routed through the graduate
+              school rather than the department</td>
+            <td>December to February, once Regeneron's request arrives</td>
+            <td class="nw">Requests go to institutions each December</td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>ARCS Foundation Scholar Awards</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">Amount, duration and even the citizenship rule are set chapter by
+              chapter; there is no national figure. US citizens or permanent residents.</span></td>
+            <td>The chapter notifies the graduate division, which coordinates departmental selection.
+              <strong>Students do not apply to ARCS at all.</strong></td>
+            <td>Spring, for the following academic year</td>
+            <td class="nw">No national deadline<br /><span class="sub">chapter-specific</span></td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>ASCB Porter Prizes for Research Excellence</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">$3,000 for the graduate prize, $5,000 for the postdoctoral one. ASCB
+              membership required; two support letters and a meeting abstract.</span></td>
+            <td>Either &mdash; candidates may self-apply or be nominated, with identical documentation.
+              The companion <strong>Merton Bernfield Memorial Award</strong> ($1,000) works the same way but
+              requires the nominator to be a member too.</td>
+            <td>None required; letters need about four weeks</td>
+            <td class="nw">Historically end of June<br /><span class="sub">exact date not currently posted</span></td>
+          </tr>
+          <tr>
+            <td><strong>Science &amp; SciLifeLab Prize for Young Scientists</strong>
+              <span class="sub2">$30,000 grand prize, $10,000 per category, and publication of the winning
+              essay in <em>Science</em>. Molecular Medicine is the natural category for an infection or
+              immunity thesis.</span></td>
+            <td>Direct application &mdash; a 1,000-word essay on the thesis</td>
+            <td>None</td>
+            <td class="nw">Historically mid-July<br /><span class="sub">for recent graduates, not current students</span></td>
+          </tr>
+        </tbody>
+      </table>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="small">
+    <h2>Travel, technique and professional development</h2>
+    <p class="lede">Small money, low competition, and almost entirely unclaimed. Several of these are
+      effectively automatic for anyone who has already paid society dues and submitted an abstract. They
+      do not substitute for stipend support, but they are what pays for the meeting where the next
+      project starts, or the ten weeks in someone else's lab learning the method the thesis needs.</p>
+    <div class="tablewrap">
+      <table class="plain">
