+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="gone">
+    <h2>Discontinued, dormant, or unreachable from here</h2>
+    <p class="lede">These still appear on funding lists, university pages and older advice. Several were
+      significant sources of support for exactly the students who can least afford to lose a cycle, and
+      two of them are still being recommended by advisers working from memory.</p>
+    <div class="foot">
+      <p class="flag"><strong>Ford Foundation Fellowships &mdash; all three levels discontinued, not just the
+        postdoctoral one.</strong> The final competition across predoctoral, dissertation and postdoctoral
+        tracks was 2023, with a limited set of awards in 2024 and the programme winding down by 2028. The
+        National Academies' Ford pages now return 404. The common belief that the predoctoral and
+        dissertation competitions survived the postdoctoral wind-down is wrong.</p>
+      <p class="flag"><strong>NIH F31-Diversity &mdash; expired and not reissued.</strong> PA-23-271 was archived in
+        February 2025, and when NIH reissued the fellowship family in June 2025 it published an F31, an
+        F32, an F33 and two F30s with no diversity counterpart. NIH issued no explicit discontinuation
+        notice, which is why some institute pages &mdash; NIAID's among them &mdash; still list it as available.
+        Published analysis counts 405 F31 awards affected by the 2025 terminations, two-thirds of them
+        F31-Diversity.</p>
+      <p class="flag"><strong>EPA STAR graduate fellowships &mdash; ended.</strong> The final cohort was selected under
+        the 2015 solicitation; EPA's current page states the resource is no longer available. What EPA
+        now offers graduate students is an NSF-partnered residency, not a fellowship competition.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Josephine de K&aacute;rm&aacute;n &mdash; no longer a national award.</strong> The trust moved to the
+        Pasadena Community Foundation in 2023, the amount rose to $28,000, and eligibility narrowed to
+        students at eleven named California institutions. Any list describing it as nationally open is
+        out of date, as is the old dekarman.org domain.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Microsoft Research PhD Fellowship &mdash; restructured.</strong> It is now the Microsoft
+        Research Fellowship: proposal-driven, scoped to named research challenges, open to PhD students,
+        postdocs and faculty alike, and paid as a one-time institutional gift of $17,000 to $47,000
+        depending on region rather than as multi-year stipend support.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Not national, despite appearances:</strong> the Burroughs Wellcome Graduate Diversity
+        Enrichment Program is restricted to PhD students at North Carolina institutions and pays $5,000
+        across two years; Knight-Hennessy funds only Stanford degrees; and GEM, GFSD and ARCS all require
+        your institution to be a member or partner.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>AAI Careers in Immunology Fellowship Program &mdash; dormant.</strong> The most recent cohort was 2024, the programme page has been removed and now returns a 404, and it no longer appears on AAI's award deadline listing; only the recipient pages survive. Its loss removes the only immunology-specific predoctoral salary mechanism, and leaves AAI offering graduate students the two no-cost trainee meeting awards and nothing else. The AAI&ndash;Thermo Fisher Trainee Achievement Award went the same way.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Dormant or unverifiable:</strong> the Gates Millennium Scholars programme is closed, and
+        even when it ran, graduate funding was available only to continuing scholars; the UNCF/Merck
+        graduate and dissertation fellowship has had no open cycle since 2014 and no notice of
+        discontinuation; ASM's Robert D. Watkins Graduate Research Fellowship and Raymond W. Sarber Award
+        have no current cycle; the Michelson Philanthropies &amp; <em>Science</em> Prize for Immunology ended with the
+        AAAS partnership; the NVIDIA Graduate Fellowship has posted no 2027&ndash;28 cycle; the Quad Fellowship
+        lists future dates as to be announced; and Autism Speaks' Dennis Weatherstone Predoctoral
+        Fellowship has no traceable current cycle.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Not available from a US institution:</strong> the Gates Foundation concluded its
+        fellowship and internship programmes in 2021 and funds no graduate research; Wellcome requires a
+        host organisation in the UK, Ireland or an eligible low- or middle-income country, and its
+        eligible list narrows further from October 2026. Neither is a route for a student here.</p>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="method">
+    <h2>Method and maintenance</h2>
+    <p class="lede">Every entry was checked against the sponsor's own page on 22 September 2026 rather
+      than against aggregators, which are the usual source of stale deadlines and superseded award
+      amounts. Where two sources disagreed, the sponsor's page won &mdash; and where the sponsor's own pages
+      disagreed with each other, that is said here rather than quietly resolved.</p>
+    <div class="foot">
+      <p><strong>Deadlines are computed, not typed.</strong> Each award stores its recurring pattern &mdash; a
+        fixed calendar date, or a rule such as "the second Friday in November" &mdash; and the page resolves
+        the next occurrence when you load it. The dates therefore stay correct into future cycles without
+        anyone editing this file. What will drift is the money and the eligibility fine print, so treat
+        the sponsor link as authoritative and this page as the thing that tells you a deadline is coming.
+        Two programmes set their dates freshly in each solicitation rather than following a rule &mdash; the
+        NSF GRFP, which moved three weeks earlier this year, and NDSEG &mdash; so confirm those two directly.</p>
+      <p><strong>Three corrections worth stating outright.</strong> The HHMI Gilliam is <em>no longer</em>
+        nomination-routed: HHMI now runs an open competition with no institutional cap, and the student
+        and adviser apply as a pair. Ford's predoctoral and dissertation tracks ended alongside the
+        postdoctoral one rather than surviving it. And the widely repeated story that NIH restricted
+        fellowship eligibility for non-citizens in 2025 traces to a four-day typo in five reissued
+        NOFOs, corrected by NOT-OD-25-126 &mdash; a correction that ran in the <em>restrictive</em> direction. The
+        standing NRSA rule, unchanged, is citizens, non-citizen nationals and permanent residents.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Left unresolved on purpose.</strong> NSF's GRFP solicitation says "less than one
+        academic year completed" while NSF's own FAQ says "not more than one academic year" &mdash; they differ
+        exactly at the boundary a second-year applicant cares about, so verify with GRFP programme staff
+        rather than trusting either. The Burroughs Wellcome CASI 2027 cycle is unposted and four BWF pages
+        contradict one another. And the July 2026 DHS rule replacing duration of status with a fixed
+        four-year admission period for F and J students took effect on 15 September 2026 and has been
+        reported to be in litigation; international students should check its operative status before
+        planning a timeline around it.</p>
+      <p><strong>What is deliberately excluded.</strong> One-off calls, programmes with no verifiable current
+        cycle, awards requiring a conferred doctorate or an independent appointment (collected separately
+        above), institutional fellowships that are really recruitment vehicles for a single university,
+        and programmes open only to undergraduates or medical students.</p>
+      <p><strong>Three structural facts the list makes visible.</strong> There is no predoctoral cancer
+        fellowship from any of the major cancer foundations &mdash; a striking gap given how much predoctoral
+        cancer research there is. There is now effectively no immunology-specific predoctoral fellowship
+        either: with the AAI programme dormant, students in infection and immunity compete in the open-field
+        and federal pools like everyone else, which is why the filter for that category is nearly empty and
+        should be. And the disease foundations are substantially more open to international students than
+        the federal mechanisms are: every federal award here is closed to visa holders, while most of the
+        foundation awards are not.</p>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+</main>
