+
+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="pairs">
+    <h2>Ideas that need two labs</h2>
+    <p class="lede">These do not belong to any single group, which is exactly why they tend to go
+      unproposed. Each is a thesis-sized question that becomes tractable when two sets of techniques
+      already in this department are put in the same room. Co-mentorship is also a genuinely strong
+      structure on an F31, provided the two mentors write letters that agree with each other about who
+      teaches what &mdash; and provided the student can say which lab they will defend from.</p>
+    <div class="pairs">
+      <div class="pair">
+        <span class="vs">Microbiome modelling &times; MRSA persistence</span>
+        <h5>Does the community around a coloniser predict which one turns invasive?</h5>
+        <p>Longitudinal isolate genomics says what a colonising strain became; ecological modelling of the
+          surrounding community may say why. A thesis here starts descriptive and becomes predictive, which
+          is a structure that survives the inevitable year when the mouse work does not cooperate.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="pair">
+        <span class="vs">Envelope proteolysis &times; structural biology</span>
+        <h5>A protease&ndash;adaptor complex caught mid-cycle</h5>
+        <p>The genetics and biochemistry of envelope protease activation are worked out here; what is
+          missing is the conformational trajectory. Cryo-EM of trapped intermediates converts a regulatory
+          model into a druggable mechanism, in a WHO priority pathogen, and it teaches a bacterial
+          geneticist structure.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="pair">
+        <span class="vs">Myeloid biology &times; respiratory transmission</span>
+        <h5>Does the airway myeloid compartment decide who transmits?</h5>
+        <p>Transmission models measure infectiousness; myeloid genetics can remove one macrophage subset at
+          a time. Together they ask whether an immune cell type, not just viral load, sets how much virus
+          leaves a host &mdash; a question neither approach can reach alone.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="pair">
+        <span class="vs">Translational control &times; vaccine immunology</span>
+        <h5>Is antibody durability set at the level of translation?</h5>
+        <p>Translation-factor balance decides T cell lineage commitment in culture. Human vaccination
+          cohorts measure durability but rarely mechanism. Testing whether the translational state of a
+          Tfh cell at priming predicts antibody persistence a year later connects the two, and gives an
+          RNA-trained student a legitimate immunology training plan.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="pair">
+        <span class="vs">Milk and early-life microbiome &times; neonatal pathogenesis</span>
+        <h5>Where does a newborn's resistome actually come from?</h5>
+        <p>Source-tracking methods can apportion microbial origin between milk, maternal gut and
+          environment. Applied to resistance genes rather than taxa, and paired with neonatal colonisation
+          models, a descriptive observation becomes a mechanism with an intervention point.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="pair">
+        <span class="vs">Programmable viral vectors &times; tissue macrophages</span>
+        <h5>Interferon switched off in exactly one cell type</h5>
+        <p>Cell-type-restricted vectors can deliver an immune antagonist to a single population in vivo.
+          Aimed at a defined macrophage subset, this asks which cell's interferon response actually
+          controls disease outcome &mdash; something conditional knockouts approximate but never isolate,
+          because they remove the pathway from development onward.</p>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="card section-spacer" id="howto">
+    <h2>Turning one of these into an F31</h2>
+    <p class="lede">Predoctoral applications fail structurally more often than scientifically, and the
+      structural failures are specific and avoidable. Almost none of what follows is about the science.</p>
+    <div class="foot">
+      <p><strong>The F31 is a training grant with a research plan attached, not the reverse.</strong> The
+        reviewers are asked whether this candidate, in this environment, with this sponsor, will become an
+        independent scientist. A flawless set of aims attached to a training plan that teaches nothing new
+        scores worse than good aims with a plan that names three techniques the applicant cannot yet do
+        and the person who will teach each one. Every direction on this page was chosen to sit one step
+        outside an existing strength for exactly that reason.</p>
+      <p><strong>Check the clock before the science.</strong> The single largest award a graduate student can
+        win &mdash; the NSF GRFP &mdash; accepts enrolled students only in the first year, once, with a deadline in
+        October. That means it is planned in the summer before matriculating, not after the first
+        committee meeting. The Hertz closes at year two, the Soros at year two, the Gilliam runs in years
+        two and three, and the F99/K00 wants one to two years left. Work out which windows are still open
+        before choosing what to write.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>Citizenship forks the whole list.</strong> Every federal mechanism &mdash; F31, F30,
+        F99/K00, GRFP, NDSEG, both DOE programmes &mdash; is closed to students on a visa. An international
+        student's real list is shorter but not empty, and it is worth establishing which list applies
+        before writing a page. The Gilliam is the largest multi-year award open to international students,
+        and the disease foundations are substantially more open than the government is.</p>
+      <p><strong>Propose the thing that is adjacent, not identical.</strong> A proposal that is a natural
+        continuation of what the lab already publishes reads as a strong preliminary-data section and a
+        weak training plan. The most common review comment on a resubmitted F31 is not that the science
+        was wrong; it is that the candidate could already do all of it.</p>
+      <p class="gate"><strong>The sponsor statement is half the application</strong> and is the part most often
+        left to the last week. It has to say specifically what the student will learn, from whom, what the
+        lab's funding situation is, and what happens to the project if the student leaves &mdash; and for a
+        co-mentored proposal, the two statements must describe the same division of labour. Reviewers
+        notice when they do not.</p>
+      <p><strong>Where the ideas came from.</strong> Themes and available techniques were drawn from the
+        department's own lab research profiles &mdash; the same source the grant slate and the postdoctoral
+        ideas page use. Two profiles are left out, the same two the postdoctoral page omits: one lab whose
+        principal investigator has left the institution, and one where a degree running five or six years
+        would outlast the sponsoring lab. No individuals are named anywhere on this page, by design: the
+        themes are meant to be recognisable to the people working in them without reading as an
+        instruction to anyone.</p>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+</main>
